<Wiki
  title="puv load"
  description="Install a project-local tool in its own environment, separate from the app solve."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>load</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv load</code> installs a project-local tool. The tool gets its own environment. It
    does not share a solver with the application dependencies from
    <a href="/wiki/commands/add"><code>puv add</code></a>.
  </p>

  <h2>One tool</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv load phpstan/phpstan</pre>
  <p>
    The environment lives at <code>.puv/tools/phpstan/</code>. The app’s
    <code>[dependencies]</code> do not gain a <code>phpstan/phpstan</code> line because of this
    command. The manifest can still name project tools under <code>[tool-dependencies]</code>:
  </p>
  <pre class="block">[tool-dependencies]
phpstan/phpstan = "^2.0"</pre>
  <p>
    That table is part of <a href="/wiki/files">files</a>. A global install of the same package,
    with a shim in <code>~/.local/bin</code>, is
    <a href="/wiki/commands/tool"><code>puv tool install</code></a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it is separate</h2>
  <p>
    PHPStan’s own dependencies are solved for PHPStan. They are not solved together with
    <code>symfony/console</code> or <code>phpunit/phpunit</code>.
    <code>puv add --dev phpstan/phpstan</code> would put it in the app graph.
    <code>load</code> does not.
  </p>
</Wiki>
